cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ft-algorithms or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "ft-algorithms: factoring and chemistry on a simulated fault-tolerant quantum computer"
abstract: >-
  Shor's algorithm (full modular exponentiation, textbook and windowed arithmetic) and molecular
  phase estimation compiled to Clifford+T+Toffoli and run end to end on a simulated rotated
  surface-code machine whose logical error channels (idling, lattice-surgery merges, the surgery
  CNOT) were measured by circuit-level simulation with stabilizer-qec and checked by a composition
  test; ftsim, a Rust state-vector simulator stratified by fault count, runs the programs natively,
  from Python and in the browser. Results are success probabilities against code distance, error
  budgets, and extrapolations to RSA-2048 and FeMoco compared with published estimates.
type: software
authors:
